DZ_FINDINGS = 'ALGERIA (DZ): findings for cl-stack-calendars#44\n\nSTATUTE CHAIN. All texts were read in the JORADP French edition from joradp.dz; PDFs are cached in ~/.cache/cl-stack-calendars/dz/jo-fr-*.pdf. The 1963, 1966 and 1968 issues are scans, so I read them from page images.\n- Loi n° 63-278 du 26 juillet 1963: JORADP n° 53 of 2 Aug 1963, pp. 776-777, https://www.joradp.dz/FTP/JO-FRANCAIS/1963/F1963053.pdf\n  - Paragraph I: 1 May, 5 July (Indépendance et FLN), 1 Nov.\n  - Paragraph II: Fitr 2 days, Adha 1 day, Awal Moharram 1, Achoura 1, Mawlid 1, 1 January 1.\n- Ordonnance n° 66-153 du 8 juin 1966: JORADP n° 52 of 17 Jun 1966, p. 602, https://www.joradp.dz/FTP/JO-FRANCAIS/1966/F1966052.pdf\n  - Adds \'Dix-neuf juin\' (19 June, anniversary of the 1965 \'redressement révolutionnaire\') to paragraph I.\n  - This day was a legal holiday until 2004. python-holidays 0.109 and timeanddate both miss it, and the current starter calendar lacks it too.\n- Ordonnance n° 68-419 du 26 juin 1968: JORADP n° 56 of 12 Jul 1968, p. 836, https://www.joradp.dz/FTP/JO-FRANCAIS/1968/F1968056.pdf\n  - Adha goes from 1 day to 2.\n  - Wikipedia fr writes this as \'68/149\', which is a typo for 68-419.\n- Loi n° 05-06 du 26 avril 2005: JORADP n° 30 of 27 Apr 2005, p. 5, https://www.joradp.dz/FTP/JO-FRANCAIS/2005/F2005030.pdf\n  - Paragraph I becomes 1 May, 5 July (fête de l\'Indépendance) and 1 Nov.\n  - This removes 19 June from 2005 on and drops \'et du F.L.N.\' from 5 July.\n- Council of Ministers, 27 Dec 2017: President Bouteflika made Yennayer (12 January) a paid day off from 12 Jan 2018.\n  - The APS copy was not retrieved; the date rests on secondary sources (Wikipedia fr, TSA, Le Monde 2018-01-12).\n- Loi n° 18-12 du 2 juillet 2018: JORADP n° 46 of 29 Jul 2018, p. 38, https://www.joradp.dz/FTP/JO-FRANCAIS/2018/F2018046.pdf\n  - Adds \'Amenzu n Yennayer ... correspondant au 12 janvier: 1 jour\' to paragraph II.\n  - Search results cite JO n° 40; the correct issue is n° 46.\n- Loi n° 23-10 du 26 juin 2023: JORADP n° 43 of 27 Jun 2023, p. 26, https://www.joradp.dz/FTP/JO-FRANCAIS/2023/F2023043.pdf\n  - Aïd El Fitr goes to 3 days and Aïd El Adha to 3 days.\n  - It was published the day before Aïd El Adha 1444 (Wed 28 Jun 2023), so Adha 2023 already had 3 days (28-30 Jun 2023; timeanddate and python-holidays agree).\n  - The first 3-day Fitr was 2024 (10-12 Apr).\n- No 2023 or later amendment changes anything else, and no amendment between 1968 and 2005 was found. The loi 05-06 recital cites the 1963 law as \'modifiée et complétée\'; the 1968 ordinance cites it without \'modifiée\'.\n\nISSUE ITEMS.\n- Good Friday is NOT an Algerian holiday: it is absent from the 1963 text. Easter Monday is not a general public holiday either. Art. 3 of loi 63-278 lists Lundi de Pâques, Ascension, Lundi de Pentecôte, 15 août and 25 décembre only for personnel of Christian confession, and art. 4 lists Roch Hachana, Yom Kippour and Pessah only for Jewish personnel. The starter\'s \':easter "Vendredi saint"\' and \':easter "Lundi de Pâques"\' entries should be removed. python-holidays keeps these days in separate CHRISTIAN and HEBREW categories, not PUBLIC.\n- Eid lengths by era:\n  - Fitr: 2 days from 1963 to 2023, 3 days from 2024.\n  - Adha: 1 day 1963-1968, 2 days from 1968 to Adha 2022, 3 days from Adha 2023.\n  - python-holidays agrees for 2000+.\n- Awal Moharram, Achoura (10 Moharram) and El-Mawlid Ennabawi are 1 day each throughout, by the declared Hijri dates.\n- 19 June (2000-2004) is missing from every secondary source.\n- In 2000-2004, 5 July was named \'fête de l\'Indépendance et du F.L.N.\'.\n\nDECLARED ISLAMIC DATES. The authority is the Commission nationale des croissants (lunar crescents committee) of the Ministère des Affaires religieuses et des Wakfs. The days off are confirmed by joint communiqués of the Ministry of Labour and the DGFP, carried by APS.\n- Primary sources: APS articles 2017-2026. Older aps.dz URLs now return 404, so I read those from Wayback snapshots; 2025-2026 articles are live on www.aps.dz/fr. Cached as ~/.cache/cl-stack-calendars/dz/aps/<id>.html.\n- An APS announcement often names only the weekday or the Hijri day (\'jeudi prochain\', \'1er Moharam 1440\'). I resolved the Gregorian date from the announcement date and checked it against ICOP.\n- Secondary source: ICOP\'s \'OFFICIAL First Day in Different Countries\' lists for Algeria (astronomycenter.net/icop/{shw,hej,muh,raa}NN.html), which cover Hijri 1424-1448 with gaps. Each feast date is derived as Fitr = 1 Shawwal, Adha = 1 Dhu al-Hijja + 9, Achoura = 1 Muharram + 9, Mawlid = 1 Rabi I + 11.\n- Wherever APS and ICOP overlap, they agree.\n- timeanddate.com/holidays/algeria is used only where nothing else exists (mostly 2000-2006 Eids and Muharram). It lacks Mawlid and Achoura before 2015, lacks 19 June, and shows only 2 days for Adha 2026, although APS announced 3 (Wed-Fri 27-29 May 2026). It also differs from ICOP on some dates. I preferred ICOP, and the differences are listed in each year\'s notes.\n- Where no source at all gives Mawlid, Achoura or Muharram for a year, the day is entered as an ESTIMATE from python-holidays 0.109 (tabular), with its own doc entry and a note. Treat these as placeholders.\n- Confidence: a year is marked \'primary\' only when every Islamic day of that year has an APS source; otherwise \'secondary\'. 2027 is not included: nothing had been announced as of 2026-11-28.\n\nAD HOC. Election days are not \'fêtes légales\' and are not in DZ_YEARS. They are listed in DZ_ADHOC:\n- 2 Jul 2026 legislative: an \'autorisation spéciale d\'absence\' (Radio Algérienne node 89434).\n- 4 May 2017 and 12 Jun 2021: timeanddate lists them as \'Election Day\'; unconfirmed. Weekends: Thursday-Friday until 2009-08-13, then Friday-Saturday, per the existing weekends.lisp. No weekend day was made a working day in any source I found.\n\npython-holidays 0.109 vs decree: it misses 19 June 2000-2004, otherwise matches the fixed list, and marks all Islamic dates as estimated.\n'
